        ":question/problem": "![](images/c4/c4aa91668440687bbae4b1f85672f5cbaf7ce00d978049c7558eed99b7361d1a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨3t-{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=1.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3-3{t}^{2},\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(3-3{t}^{2})}^{2}+{(6t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9-18{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+18{t}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =3({t}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+1-[\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+(-1)]) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{3}+1+\\frac{1}{3}+1) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
